      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes **how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure**. \n\nHere\u0027s what it covers:\n\n- **Journal mechanism**: Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records that file\u0027s prior state \u2014 either its previous content (if it existed) or the fact that it did not exist \u2014 into an in-memory write journal.\n\n- **Rollback on failure**: If an agent run fails (due to exceeding turn caps, unrecoverable errors, or denied writes), the journal can reverse every recorded write in reverse order: restoring previous content for files that existed before, and deleting any newly created files.\n\n- **All-or-nothing semantics**: This approach gives each run atomic write semantics without requiring a database transaction \u2014 the journal itself acts as the transaction log, kept in memory for the duration of one run.\n\n- **Query agent note**: The Query agent (which has no write tool) never uses the rollback capability, though the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library.",
